TEXT 80 -56 Left 2 ;6 kHz reference and a CD4013B toggle flip-flop produce approximately 12 kHz VCO output.
TEXT 80 80 Left 2 ;5 V supply and CD4046B timing network
TEXT 80 1060 Left 2 ;External R1, R2, C1 set the oscillator range; PC1 and PC2 are chip outputs.
TEXT 2550 520 Left 2 ;QN (pin 2) feeds D (pin 5); Q (pin 1) returns to CD4046 pin 3.
TEXT 80 1120 Left 2 !.param FREF=6k
TEXT 80 1152 Left 2 !.tran 0 120m 0 500n
TEXT 80 1184 Left 2 !.meas tran T1 WHEN V(VCO)=2.5 RISE=700
TEXT 80 1216 Left 2 !.meas tran T2 WHEN V(VCO)=2.5 RISE=701
TEXT 80 1248 Left 2 !.meas tran F_VCO PARAM 1/(T2-T1)
TEXT 80 1312 Left 2 !.include ..\..\LTspice\Models\Community\cd4000.lib
TEXT 80 -336 Left 3 ;#60 Divide-by-Two PLL
TEXT 80 -272 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SS7z8WsXPMk
TEXT 80 -224 Left 2 ;A feedback loop locks the CD4046 VCO to the reference through a divide-by-two stage.
